# Finite independent review of the Notes publication correction

The frozen 504-artifact correction, original 325-artifact trash stage and prior 37-artifact independent review were authenticated before and after local execution. No source, production, requirements or prior result file was changed.

All **18 local cases pass** with zero skips: seven original reviewer bodies retargeted only by explicit import prefixes, the author's exact seven adjacent bodies, and four new held-out controls. The new controls cover field changes without input events, preservation of the committed identity for a new-note Save while a later draft remains visible, older second-refresh responses after a newer search, and immutable Trash/Restore primitives across the queue await. The original two failures now pass; both refresh-await publication controls pass. Failed persistence, disk reopen, native restore and bounds cases remain independently represented.

The seven-case replay executes one new authenticated released Joplin helper context/top-level restore call. Eleven final item projections match five fields each (55 scalar assertions). The nine exact released slices run through the unchanged owned in-memory SQL/load/save adapters and fixed clock. Complete original application, original database, synchronization and GUI executions are zero. The author’s earlier 55 tests and historical original counts are separate evidence, not new reviewer executions.

Source review confirms the correction changes only `client.mjs` and `server.mjs`: Save captures editor generation, input revision and all four field values; both refresh reads check their request generation; the new notebook Trash/Restore actions copy action/ID/revision/confirmation before queueing. The native algorithms, serialization and upstream source/helper bytes remain unchanged. It does not provide a universal input ownership or lifecycle cancellation contract for earlier Notes actions.

## Incomplete browser attempt

One owned Chrome preview served the exact corrected client and Markdown module with a small owned HTML/API relay to the frozen actual shared HTTP host. The note opened and a genuine completed Save response was held after disk commit (revision 2). Notebook selection was observed. Clicking trash opened a native JavaScript confirmation, but the browser bridge stalled. The ordinary confirmation handler, documented CDP dialog alternative and manual tab close all failed at the bridge's focus command. The backend did not receive notebook-trash. These are preserved tool failures, not application failures or completed browser acceptance. The private host was closed and its owned temporary directory removed. The ephemeral tab should close at turn cleanup; successful manual closure is not claimed.

Browser source fingerprints are captured before and after. No remote account, actual credential or user port 4311 was used. The relay's `restart` option was not invoked, so no new real process-restart proof is claimed. File-backed reopen in the local corpus remains separately scoped.

Licensing/provenance remain source-assisted Joplin Desktop 3.6.14, commit `7e2765a3857754d12dbadea442b60ceaf9d4b23d`, AGPL-3.0-or-later. Exact upstream/manual/license bytes and initial negative proofs stay in their immutable manifest references. No original carrier is copied. Native metadata equality is finite helper evidence; no complete product, security, timing, memory or superiority claim is made.

No confirmed application fault remains in this finite review. Actual browser acceptance remains open for the parent to complete when browser control is available.
